From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iceland <iceland@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:36:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/30] gpu_display: iceland gvm: server-side frame on KWin,
 window close reported instead of a hard VM exit

Bind zxdg_decoration_manager_v1 when the compositor offers it (KWin; Mutter
does not) and ask for a server-side frame so the crosvm window gets a title
bar on Plasma (CROSVM_GVM_NO_SSD=1 disables it). A compositor close request
now prints GVM-WINDOW-CLOSE instead of exiting the VM without a guest
shutdown; the iceland-vms supervisor shuts the guest down cleanly.
CROSVM_GVM_CLOSE=exit restores the upstream behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gpu_display/build.rs                          |   1 +
 .../protocol/xdg-decoration-unstable-v1.xml   | 176 ++++++++++++++++++
 gpu_display/src/display_wl.c                  |  36 +++-
 3 files changed, 212 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 gpu_display/protocol/xdg-decoration-unstable-v1.xml

diff --git a/gpu_display/build.rs b/gpu_display/build.rs
index 3a0e30e..ecbce4e 100644
--- a/gpu_display/build.rs
+++ b/gpu_display/build.rs
@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@ fn build_wayland() {
         "xdg-shell",
         "viewporter",
         "virtio-gpu-metadata-v1",
+        "xdg-decoration-unstable-v1",
     ] {
         build.file(compile_protocol(protocol, &out_dir));
     }
